    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup anchored by **Kyle Tucker**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who lead the board with efficiency scores of 75.81, 75.10, and 74.56, respectively. **Kyle Tucker** benefits significantly from a soft matchup against Lorenzen, whose 4.71 xERA provides an ideal environment for a breakout performance. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** draws a positive platoon edge and, perhaps more crucially, faces a pitcher with a slow delivery, boosting his stolen base potential\u2014a priority metric for our squad. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Andy Pages** are both set up for success against Imai and Lorenzen, with the former buoyed by an 8% lineup order bonus as he sets the table at the top of the lineup.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Jorge Polanco**, who remains the most efficient alternative but fell just short of a start due to a slight park penalty and marginal platoon disadvantage against Lugo. While **Miguel Vargas** boasts an elite .406 xwOBA, his matchup against Tolle remains suboptimal for our current roster construction. Managers should monitor the 45% rain risk for both **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** in their games against Boyd. While both are projected as mid-tier starts, these weather alerts coupled with the difficulty of facing a left-handed arm warrant close attention before first pitch. Furthermore, **Drake Baldwin** faces the toughest test of the day against Skenes; while his start is secured, the 33% rain risk adds a layer of volatility to a matchup already hindered by the pitcher's elite skill profile.",
